  "description": "The v0.4.0 Step 3 Ed25519 receipt vector (AC9/AC10): the fixed seed (32 bytes of 0x01) derives the SAME RFC 8032 keypair in Go and Node (the mirror imports the seed via JWK d; Node generateKeyPairSync seed is not RFC 8032 compliant). Go canonicalizes the memory_approved payload and the unsigned envelope, hashes them, signs the unsigned envelope with the seed and digests the complete receipt - every computed byte must equal the pinned vector (canonicalPayloadBytes, payloadHash, unsignedEnvelopeBytes, signature, completeReceiptBytes, receiptHash, keyId). Node verifies Go's bytes (AC9); Node canonicalizes and signs the same payload and Go verifies it (AC10) - the vector IS the cross-runtime contract. The reason carries an & (no HTML escaping) and a \" (JSON escaping); roles are canonically sorted. Accounting correctness: NOT ASSERTED.",
